From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:20:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/25] sglang DSA: correct how patch 2a's evidence is
 described

The previous commit described 2a as untested in isolation and left the IndexShare
table calling it "Unknown". Both were wrong. The error came from inferring
evidence strength from verification mechanics -- 2a is checked by source-grep
rather than bytecode, because it changes an expression and introduces no new
identifier -- instead of reading the kit that recorded how it was established.

2a was localized by observation, not by argument: a py-spy dump caught a BUSY rank
blocked inside dsa_backend on .max().item() while IDLE peers had already advanced
into the next collective. After the fix no rank appears in dsa_backend in a dump
again and PD warmup passes on all 8 ranks. Fix A2 (dropping the two unconditional
.cpu() syncs on the same branch) was forced by experiment: with A alone, the hang
persists. Over-allocating page-table columns was verified safe by walking every
consumer, and the sync-free idiom is established in-tree three times.

Upstream non-coverage was verified per-diff and is now stated: #31683 does not
touch this file's max_seqlen_k path; #32209/#32196 vote on graph capture, which a
host-side sync is invisible to; merged #29798 repaired the GLOBAL eager path and
never anticipated per-rank asymmetric entry.

The IndexShare table now reads "No" for 2a with the reason, rather than "Unknown".

Headers re-verified by a real --fuzz=0 apply into a pristine v0.5.15.post1 tree in
prerequisite order: all three clean, 9 files modified.

